---
import RelatedLinks from '../../RelatedLinks.astro';
---
<main>
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--mint" id="overview">
    <div class="wrap page-hero__grid">
      <div class="page-hero__copy reveal">
        <span class="ey">PunchOut integrations</span>
        <h1>Connect buyer procurement to your Shopify storefront.</h1>
        <p class="lead">PunchOut Central sits between an enterprise buyer's procurement system and the supplier's existing Shopify or Shopify Plus store. Explore the storefront, buyer systems and protocols involved.</p>
        <div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss an integration &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="#details">Explore connection paths &darr;</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual reveal">
        <div class="hero-visual__label"><span>Connection roles</span><b>Buyer to supplier</b></div>
        <div class="visual-flow">
          <div class="visual-step is-accent"><i>01</i><span><strong>Procurement system</strong><small>Buyer starts and approves</small></span></div>
          <div class="visual-step is-lavender"><i>02</i><span><strong>PunchOut Central</strong><small>Connects the workflow</small></span></div>
          <div class="visual-step is-peach"><i>03</i><span><strong>Shopify store</strong><small>Supplier catalog and order</small></span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="sec" id="details">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Choose a starting point</span><h2>Three parts of a PunchOut integration.</h2><p class="lead">A buyer system is not a storefront, and a protocol is not a procurement product. Each part has a separate role.</p></div>
      <div class="related-grid">
        <a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/procurement-systems/"><span>Buyer side</span><h3>Procurement systems</h3><p>Review the buyer platforms in the supported ecosystem and what must be confirmed for each connection.</p><b>Explore buyer systems &rarr;</b></a>
        <a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/shopify/"><span>Supplier side</span><h3>Shopify integration</h3><p>Use your existing Shopify or Shopify Plus store as the catalog and destination for approved orders.</p><b>Explore Shopify &rarr;</b></a>
        <a class="related-card reveal" href="/how-it-works/"><span>Transaction</span><h3>Six-stage workflow</h3><p>See how cart return, buyer approval, purchase order, Shopify order and invoice relate.</p><b>Follow the workflow &rarr;</b></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="protocols">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Procurement protocols</span><h2>Support for cXML and OCI.</h2><p class="lead">The buyer's requirements determine which protocol and connection settings are needed. Both are implemented in PunchOut Central.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">01</span><h3>cXML PunchOut</h3><p>Connect cXML buyer sessions and cart return to the supplier catalog and wider procurement transaction.</p><a href="/integrations/cxml/">Explore cXML &rarr;</a></article>
        <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">02</span><h3>OCI PunchOut</h3><p>Connect OCI catalog launch and cart return to an existing Shopify storefront.</p><a href="/integrations/oci/">Explore OCI &rarr;</a></article>
        <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">03</span><h3>Buyer-specific setup</h3><p>Confirm the procurement system, protocol, buyer settings and test steps before a connection goes live.</p><a href="/book-demo/">Discuss requirements &rarr;</a></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="sec" id="proof">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">One operating view</span><h2>Manage connections and transactions centrally.</h2><p class="lead">Connect more than one enterprise buyer to a store, or manage multiple Shopify stores and buyer connections from one platform.</p></div>
      <div class="metrics-row">
        <article class="metric reveal"><strong>Buyer settings</strong><span>Configure the store and catalog access for each buyer connection.</span></article>
        <article class="metric reveal"><strong>Order boundary</strong><span>Return the cart for approval; create the store order after the approved PO.</span></article>
        <article class="metric metric--dark reveal"><strong>Visibility</strong><span>Track transaction stages, issues and reporting in one place.</span></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <RelatedLinks source="/integrations/" heading="Explore the integration paths" />
  <section class="page-cta"><div class="wrap reveal"><span class="ey">Bring your requirements</span><h2>Map the buyer system to your store.</h2><p class="lead">Tell us which procurement system your buyer uses and which Shopify store you want to connect.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss your integration &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="/pricing/">See pricing</a></div></div></section>
</main>
